title VBC Query: Contact Navigation (Passive Read)

participant "Applet VBC" as Applet
participant "VBC (Logic)" as VBC
participant "Contact BC" as Contact
participant "DPS.Profile" as ProfileAPI
participant "DPS.RnP" as RNP

note over VBC: User navigates to Contact view\n(Query event is triggered on VBC)

alt [TMO Profile Id and TMO MultiPartyCompany are EMPTY]
    
    VBC -> ProfileAPI: GET /profile (email=Contact.Email)
    ProfileAPI --> VBC: profile data or None
    
    opt [Profile FOUND and contains relatedParties with Client ID]
        note over VBC: Verify if relatedParties (adminCompany)\ncontains Client ID (from Contact join)
        VBC -> Contact: populate [TMO Profile Id]\nand [TMO MultiPartyCompany] on BC
    end
    note over VBC: If profile or entity is missing, NO POST is made.\nFields remain empty.
    
else [TMO Profile Id is POPULATED, but TMO MultiPartyCompany is EMPTY]
    
    VBC -> ProfileAPI: GET /profile/{profileId}
    ProfileAPI --> VBC: profile data
    
    opt [Profile contains relatedParties with Client ID]
        note over VBC: Verify if relatedParties (adminCompany)\ncontains Client ID
        VBC -> Contact: populate [TMO MultiPartyCompany] on BC
    end
    note over VBC: Missing entity is NOT added via POST.\nField remains empty.

else [Both fields on Contact BC are POPULATED]
    note over VBC: No background sync with DPS.Profile needed
end

== Fetch permissions for Applet ==

alt [Both TMO Profile Id and TMO MultiPartyCompany are POPULATED]
    VBC -> RNP: GET /permissions\n(query: profileId AND multipartyCompanyId)
    RNP --> VBC: list of permissions for THIS company
    VBC --> Applet: Render data (or empty rows if none)
else [Any of the fields is still EMPTY]
    note over VBC: Skip RNP call (missing context)
    VBC --> Applet: Render empty VBC view
end

